\title{LocalVolatility: Option Pricing Under Local and Stochastic Volatility}
\description{
Finite-difference PDE solvers and Monte Carlo engines for pricing European and American options under local and stochastic volatility models, implemented in C++ via 'Rcpp'. Includes one-dimensional Crank-Nicolson solvers with local volatility surfaces, two-dimensional Yanenko operator-splitting solvers for quanto/ADR products (equity plus FX), Heston (1993) \doi{10.1093/rfs/6.2.327} stochastic volatility solvers (closed-form characteristic function and PDE), and a four-dimensional Monte Carlo engine for double-Heston quanto options with Longstaff-Schwartz \doi{10.1093/rfs/14.1.113} least-squares regression for American exercise. Supports Tavella-Randall nonuniform grids, penalty-projection for early exercise, antithetic variates, and 'std::thread' parallelism for calibration-optimised batch pricing.
}
